        "action": "CORRECTED_PREFERRED_TERM_SPELLING",
        "changes": "Corrected the misspelling 'Naphtyl' -> 'Naphthyl' in preferred_term. This is not a regrounding: the record stays on CHEBI:32918 and denotes the same substance, and the record already carried '1-naphthylacetic acid' as a synonym, so the correct spelling was never in doubt. It matters now because kg-microbe overwrites an ontology term's canonical name from a symmetric SSSOM row, so this typo was published as the KG's name for CHEBI:32918 '1-naphthaleneacetic acid'. The raw misspelling is kept as a RAW_TEXT synonym so any source string still resolves — MAPPING_SEMANTICS warns that renaming a record removes the raw label downstream consumers match on, and keeping it as a synonym is what avoids that.",
