        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "anchor_cas_hydrate_records",
          "notes": "D-(+)-melezitose monohydrate is a hydrate/salt with its own CAS and no exact ChEBI term; anchored to the parent CHEBI:6731 'melezitose' by narrowMatch per MAPPING_SEMANTICS.md Section 3 step 2. monohydrate of melezitose"
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "MIM curation (#342)",
          "notes": "mapping_quality NARROW_MATCH -> CLOSE_MATCH, predicate skos:narrowMatch -> skos:closeMatch. narrowMatch asserts this record is *narrower in meaning* than CHEBI:6731 ('melezitose') — a subsumption ChEBI itself denies: it files hydrates under CHEBI:35505 'hydrate', never under the anhydrous compound, which is not an ancestor even transitively. A hydrate is a distinct substance containing the anhydrous form, not a specialization of it. closeMatch claims similarity without subsumption. The ontology_id and the record's own identifier are unchanged."
        },
        {
          "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
          "source": "MIM curation (#901); PubChem CID 16217716; ChEBI:6731",
          "notes": "PubChem CID 16217716 formula C18H34O17, CAS synonym 10030-67-8 and stereochemical InChI agree with this monohydrate. PubChem parent CID 92817 agrees with anhydrous CHEBI:6731 (C18H32O16). Archived 2026-11-01 OLS and pinned local ChEBI searches found no exact monohydrate term. CHEBI:183824 is anhydrous with different stereochemistry and is not a substitute. Current MAPPING_SEMANTICS section 3 and its form-of ruling require skos:broadMatch plus B1 identity, not subclass projection or exact parent identity. No role approval is implied. Sources: https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/16217716 ; https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/92817 ; https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:6731 ."
        }
      ]
    },
