        "A member of the class of pyrroles that is 1<em>H</em>-pyrrole which is substituted by chloro groups at positions 2 and 3 and by a nitro group  position 4. It is the simplest member of the pyrrolomycins, a family of natural products found in several species of the <em>Streptomyces</em> genus. The compound is active against Gram-positive and Gram-negative bacteria and some genera of fungi."
